---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MoreInCategory from "../components/MoreInCategory.astro";
import { authorSchema, authorName } from "../data/authors";
import AuthorAvatar from "../components/AuthorAvatar.astro";
import QuickPicks from "../components/QuickPicks.astro";
import PlanTheJob from "../components/PlanTheJob.astro";
import AuthorBio from "../components/AuthorBio.astro";
import { amazonLink } from "../data/affiliate";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";
import SocialProof from "../components/SocialProof.astro";
import productImages from "../data/product-images.json";
import { pageDates } from "../data/dates";

const moreInCategory = [
  {
    "title": "Best Shop Vacs",
    "url": "/best-shop-vac/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Small Shop Vacs",
    "url": "/best-small-shop-vac/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Shop Vac Bags",
    "url": "/best-shop-vac-bags/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Shop Vac Filters Explained",
    "url": "/shop-vac-filters-explained/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Shop Vac vs Dust Extractor",
    "url": "/shop-vac-vs-dust-extractor/"
  },
  {
    "title": "Best Dust Collectors",
    "url": "/best-dust-collector/"
  }
];
const dates = pageDates(Astro.url.pathname, { published: "2026-11-05", modified: "2026-11-05" });
const title = "7 Best Shop Vac Attachments in 2026: Kits, Adapters and Separators by Hose Size";
const description =
  "The best shop vac attachments by hose size: 1-1/4, 1-7/8 and 2-1/2 inch kits, car detailing tools, power tool adapters and Dust Deputy vs Dustopper.";

const PRODUCTS = [
  {
    "id": "ridgid-vt2575",
    "name": "RIDGID VT2575 1-7/8 in. and 2-1/2 in. Heavy-Duty Cleaning Kit (32703)",
    "category": "12 Pieces, Fits 1-7/8 and 2-1/2 in. Hoses",
    "badge": "Best Overall Kit",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Two stainless steel extension wands, one straight and one bent, with push-button locks",
      "Hose adapters for both 1-7/8 and 2-1/2 in. hoses",
      "2-1/2 to 1-1/4 in. reducer for small hand tools",
      "Floor nozzle with squeegee, brush and carpet inserts, plus claw nozzle, crevice tool and dusting brush"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Priced like a premium kit, and retailer prices vary widely",
      "Designed around RIDGID hoses; other brands' cuffs may need checking"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The one kit to buy for a 1-7/8 or 2-1/2 inch vac: metal wands, a real floor nozzle with a squeegee, and adapters for both hose sizes.",
    "description": "The VT2575, sold under RIDGID catalog number 32703, is the kit to buy if your vac came with plastic wands and a single utility nozzle. Retailer listings describe 12 pieces: two stainless steel extension wands, one straight and one bent, with push-button locks; a master floor nozzle with squeegee, brush and carpet inserts; a dusting brush; a crevice tool; a claw nozzle; and three adapters. Those adapters are what make it work across vacs. There is a hose adapter for 2-1/2 inch hoses, a hose adapter for 1-7/8 inch hoses, and a 2-1/2 to 1-1/4 inch reducer for small hand tools. Retailers list it as compatible with most RIDGID wet/dry vacs that use either hose size. The stainless wands are the upgrade owners notice first: they do not flex like plastic and they lock rather than relying on friction. The squeegee insert is the best tool here for water on a garage floor. It is not cheap, and prices vary a lot between retailers, so it pays to compare."
  },
  {
    "id": "workshop-ws25054a",
    "name": "WORKSHOP Wet/Dry Vacs WS25054A 2-1/2 in. Homeowner/DIY Vac Attachment Kit",
    "category": "5 Pieces, 2-1/2 in.",
    "badge": "Best Budget Kit (2-1/2 in.)",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Five tools that cover most jobs: crevice, brush, wet nozzle, floor brush, claw",
      "Fits most vacs with a 2-1/2 in. hose or wand",
      "Wet nozzle for water on hard floors",
      "Much cheaper than a full RIDGID kit"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "No extension wands in the box",
      "All plastic"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The cheapest way to add the five tools a 2-1/2 inch vac is usually missing, if you already have wands.",
    "description": "WORKSHOP's WS25054A is a 5-piece homeowner kit for 2-1/2 inch hoses, and it covers the tools a big vac's stock kit usually leaves out. Retailer listings describe a flexible crevice tool, a triangle soft-bristle brush, a wet nozzle, a floor brush and a claw nozzle. The flexible crevice tool reaches behind appliances and along baseboards. The triangle brush gets into corners and vent grilles without scratching. The wet nozzle has a squeegee lip for water on concrete and tile, and the claw nozzle has teeth that agitate carpet and pull debris out of it. What it does not include is extension wands, so it assumes your vac came with them. WORKSHOP describes it as fitting most vacs with a 2-1/2 inch hose or wand, which covers most 8 gallon and larger shop vacs. For a 1-7/8 inch vac, WORKSHOP sells the same idea as the WS17854A. The tools are plastic and not as rigid as RIDGID's, but at a fraction of the VT2575's price they are the right buy for a vac that sees occasional use."
  },
  {
    "id": "ridgid-vt2534",
    "name": "RIDGID VT2534 7-Piece Auto Detailing Vacuum Hose Accessory Kit, 1-1/4 in.",
    "category": "Car Kit, 1-1/4 in. with 10 ft Hose",
    "badge": "Best Car Detailing Kit",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Includes its own 10 ft 1-1/4 in. hose, the right bore for car interiors",
      "Flexible crevice tool reaches seat rails and console gaps",
      "Soft and stiff bristle brushes for dash, vents and carpet",
      "Claw nozzle for floor mats"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Tools are sized for the kit's 1-1/4 in. hose end, not for 1-7/8 or 2-1/2 in. wands",
      "Piece count is listed as 6 or 7 depending on the retailer"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The car kit to buy for a RIDGID vac: a long, narrow hose and the small tools that big shop vacs lack.",
    "description": "The VT2534 solves the main problem with using a big shop vac on a car: the stock 2-1/2 inch hose and tools are too large to get between seats. Retailer listings describe a 10 foot dual-layer 1-1/4 inch hose, a flexible crevice tool, a soft bristle brush, a stiff bristle brush, a claw nozzle and an adapter, sold as a 7-piece kit; some listings count it as 6 pieces. The narrow hose is the key part. A 1-1/4 inch hose moves air faster than a 2-1/2 inch one, which suits fine dirt in carpet and vents, and 10 feet lets the vac stay on the driveway while you work through the back seat. RIDGID's support answer on one retailer listing says these tools fit the 1-1/4 inch hose end and will not fit RIDGID's regular 1-7/8 or 2-1/2 inch accessories, so use them on the included hose. The stiff brush is the one for floor mats and the soft one for the dash and screens. If you own a non-RIDGID vac, check that the hose cuff fits your vac's inlet before ordering."
  },
  {
    "id": "workshop-ws25052a",
    "name": "WORKSHOP Wet/Dry Vacs WS25052A 2-1/2 in. Car Cleaning Vacuum Attachment Kit",
    "category": "3 Pieces, 2-1/2 in.",
    "badge": "Best Car Kit for Big Hoses",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Plugs straight onto a 2-1/2 in. hose or wand, no reducer needed",
      "Flexible crevice tool, triangle soft brush and claw nozzle",
      "Keeps the full airflow of a large hose",
      "Inexpensive"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Only three pieces",
      "A 2-1/2 in. hose is heavy and stiff to work inside a car"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A cheap way to make a big 2-1/2 inch vac car-ready without buying a second hose.",
    "description": "The WS25052A is a 3-piece car kit for 2-1/2 inch hoses: a flexible crevice tool, a triangle soft-bristle brush and a claw nozzle, per retailer listings, and WORKSHOP says it fits most shop vacs with a 2-1/2 inch hose or wand. The point of a 2-1/2 inch car kit is that you keep the full airflow of the big hose right up to the tool. The claw nozzle has teeth that dig into carpet and upholstery, which is where most of a car's sand and grit ends up, and the flexible crevice tool bends to reach between the seat and the center console. The triangle brush is for the dashboard and door panels. The limitation is the hose itself. A 2-1/2 inch hose is heavy and stiff to manoeuvre inside a car, and it does not bend into tight footwells the way a 1-1/4 inch hose does. If you clean cars every week, the RIDGID VT2534 with its own narrow hose is easier to use. If it is a few times a year, this kit is the cheaper answer."
  },
  {
    "id": "dust-deputy-diy",
    "name": "Oneida Air Systems Dust Deputy DIY Anti-Static Retrofit Cyclone Separator (AXD001004)",
    "category": "Cyclone Separator, Bring Your Own Bucket",
    "badge": "Best Cyclone Separator",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Anti-static resin cyclone that mounts on your own bucket or bin",
      "Reducers and adapters for smaller vac hoses included",
      "Keeps most dust out of the vac's filter, so suction holds up",
      "One of the cheapest true cyclones Oneida sells"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "You supply the bucket and a sealed lid, and build the mount",
      "Oneida rates its inlet for 1-1/2 in.; big-hose vacs suit the Dust Deputy 2.5 DIY better"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The cheapest way to stop clogging a small vac's filter: a proper cyclone that drops dust into a bucket first.",
    "description": "The Dust Deputy DIY is Oneida Air Systems' basic cyclone separator, model AXD001004, and it is the add-on that most changes what a small shop vac can do. It sits between the hose and the vac, spins incoming air, and drops dust and chips into a bucket underneath before the air reaches the vac. Oneida lists it as a fixed-position, anti-static cyclone with a 1.5 inch vac inlet that you mount on your own bin; a retailer listing gives the ports as 2 inch OD tapered, 1-3/4 inch ID. Oneida's assembly manual describes reducers, adapters and O-rings for connecting smaller vac hoses to the cyclone ports. The DIY part is the bucket: you need a 5 gallon bucket with a sealed lid and you cut the hole for the cyclone's flange. Get the seal right and the vac's filter stays clean far longer, which is the main reason small vacs lose suction. For 2-1/2 inch hoses, Oneida's Dust Deputy 2.5 DIY (AXD251004) is the matching size, with tapered 2-1/2 inch ports."
  },
  {
    "id": "dustopper-pro-dt10000",
    "name": "Dustopper PRO DT10000 Low-Profile Dust Collector Kit with 90 Degree Elbows and Hose",
    "category": "Bucket-Lid Separator, 2-1/2 in., Fits 5 Gallon Buckets",
    "badge": "Best Bucket-Lid Separator",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Snaps onto a standard 5 gallon bucket, no cutting",
      "Kit includes high-flow 90 degree sweep elbows and a connection hose",
      "EPDM gasket and a grounding lug included",
      "Anti-static resin, made in the USA"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Designed for 2-1/2 in. hoses; the grounding kit is aimed at 5.0 HP and larger vacs",
      "The 99 to 99.9% efficiency figure is the maker's claim, not an independent test"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The easiest separator to set up on a big-hose vac: it is a bucket lid, and the kit includes the elbows.",
    "description": "The Dustopper PRO is a low-profile separator that replaces the lid of a standard 5 gallon bucket, and the DT10000 kit version includes the parts that make it easy to use. Listings describe high-flow 90 degree sweep elbows and a connection hose in the kit, plus an EPDM gasket for the bucket seal and a grounding lug. It is made from anti-static resin in the USA. Dustopper describes it as fitting standard 5 gallon buckets and 2-1/2 inch hoses, and the Amazon listing describes it for wet/dry shop vacs of 5 HP and up. Listings claim it removes more than 99% or more than 99.9% of typical shop dust, depending on which one you read. We have not seen an independent test of either figure, so treat it as the maker's number. Compared with the Dust Deputy DIY, the Dustopper is a lid rather than a cone, so it takes no cutting or gluing and stands lower, which matters under a bench. The Dust Deputy's tall cone is the more established design. Either one will keep a vac's filter cleaner for far longer."
  },
  {
    "id": "powertec-70376",
    "name": "POWERTEC 70376 Power Tool Vacuum Hose Kit, 10 ft x 1-1/2 in. ID",
    "category": "Power Tool Hose Kit, 3/4 to 1-1/2 in. ID Fittings",
    "badge": "Best for Power Tools",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "10 ft x 1-1/2 in. ID flexible PVC hose",
      "Quick-change fitting with four connectors: 3/4 in. ID (1-1/4 in. OD), 1 in., 1-1/4 in. and 1-1/2 in. ID",
      "2-1/4 to 2-1/2 in. ABS dust port/hose adapter",
      "Swivel fittings stop the hose fighting the tool"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "POWERTEC warns that vac port sizes vary by brand; measure before buying",
      "A 1-1/2 in. hose is for sanders and small saws, not for floor cleanup"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The kit to connect a shop vac to sanders, track saws and routers without a drawer full of tape and mismatched adapters.",
    "description": "POWERTEC's 70376 is a hose kit for the job most shop vac attachments ignore: connecting the vac to a power tool's dust port. POWERTEC lists a 10 foot, 1-1/2 inch ID flexible PVC hose, a 2-1/4 to 2-1/2 inch ABS dust port/hose adapter, and a quick-change fitting with four quick-connect fittings: 3/4 inch ID (1-1/4 inch OD), 1 inch ID, 1-1/4 inch ID and 1-1/2 inch ID. The Amazon listing describes the hose as stretching from 3 to 10 feet. Those four fittings cover the dust ports on most random orbit sanders, detail sanders, track saws, routers and miter saws, and the quick-change design means swapping tools is a push and twist rather than a struggle with a friction fit. The 1-1/2 inch hose is lighter and more flexible than a 2-1/2 inch vac hose, which matters when it hangs off a sander for an hour. POWERTEC itself warns that shop vac port sizes vary between manufacturers, so measure your vac's inlet and your tools' ports and compare them with the listed sizes before ordering."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Shop Vac Attachments",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/best-shop-vac-attachments/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What size are shop vac attachments?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Almost all shop vac attachments fit one of three nominal hose diameters: 1-1/4 inch, 1-7/8 inch or 2-1/2 inch. Small 1 to 2.5 gallon vacs and detailing hoses use 1-1/4 inch, mid-size vacs use 1-7/8 inch and most large vacs use 2-1/2 inch. Measure the outside of your wand or hose cuff to check before you order."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are shop vac attachments universal?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not fully. Friction-fit tools of the same diameter usually fit across Shop-Vac, Craftsman, Vacmaster and WORKSHOP vacs, though fit can be loose or tight. RIDGID's locking tools lock only on RIDGID hoses, and its 1-1/4 inch car kit is sized for its own hose. Hose cuffs that plug into the vac vary by brand and are the least interchangeable part."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best shop vac attachment kit?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a 1-7/8 or 2-1/2 inch vac, the RIDGID VT2575 (catalog 32703): a 12-piece kit with two stainless steel locking wands, a floor nozzle with squeegee, brush and carpet inserts, a claw nozzle, crevice tool, dusting brush and adapters for both hose sizes. On a budget, the WORKSHOP WS25054A adds five key tools for 2-1/2 inch hoses."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What attachment is best for cleaning a car?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A car kit with a flexible crevice tool, soft and stiff brushes and a claw nozzle. The RIDGID VT2534 comes with its own 10 foot 1-1/4 inch hose, which is light and reaches into footwells. For a 2-1/2 inch vac, the WORKSHOP WS25052A plugs straight on with a flexible crevice tool, a soft triangle brush and a claw nozzle."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a cyclone separator for my shop vac?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If the vac sees sawdust, drywall dust or a lot of fine debris, yes. A separator like the Dust Deputy DIY or Dustopper PRO drops most dust into a bucket before it reaches the filter, so suction holds up and filters last much longer. If you mostly vacuum water or loose debris, it adds little."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Dust Deputy or Dustopper: which is better?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Choose by hose size and space rather than efficiency claims, which we have not seen independently tested side by side. The Dust Deputy DIY has a 1.5 inch inlet and adapters that suit small vacs; the Dust Deputy 2.5 DIY suits 2-1/2 inch hoses. The Dustopper PRO is a low bucket lid for 2-1/2 inch hoses that snaps on with no cutting."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I connect a shop vac to a sander or saw?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Use a hose kit with fittings sized to tool ports, such as the POWERTEC 70376. It has a 10 foot 1-1/2 inch ID hose, quick-connect fittings from 3/4 inch to 1-1/2 inch ID and a 2-1/4 to 2-1/2 inch adapter. Measure your tool's port and your vac's inlet first, since sizes vary by brand."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Tools & Equipment",
    tags: [
      "shop vac attachments",
      "shop vac accessories",
      "shop vac attachment kit",
      "shop vac hose attachments",
      "dust deputy vs dustopper",
      "shop vac car detailing kit"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Updated November 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          The Best <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Shop Vac Attachments</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          The right attachment changes what a shop vac can do more than a bigger motor does. Here are seven kits, adapters and separators worth buying, with exact part numbers and the hose size each one fits.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#ridgid-vt2575"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Check Your Hose Size
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Shaheer Ali Khan</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Consumer Product Testing &amp; Materials Performance Specialist</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="7.9k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#hose-sizes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Three Hose Sizes</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. The 7 Best, Ranked</a>
          <a href="#adapters" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Adapters and Reducers</a>
          <a href="#core-tools" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Crevice, Claw, Squeegee, Brush</a>
          <a href="#car-kits" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Car Detailing Kits</a>
          <a href="#power-tools" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Power Tool Connections</a>
          <a href="#separators" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Dust Deputy vs Dustopper</a>
          <a href="#brands" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Brand Compatibility</a>
          <a href="#hoses-wands" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Hoses and Wands</a>
          <a href="#skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. What Not to Buy</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Most shop vacs come with a utility nozzle, a rigid crevice tool and two plastic wands, and that kit is the main reason a perfectly good vac feels clumsy. An inexpensive kit at the right hose size adds a claw nozzle for carpet, a squeegee for water, a flexible crevice tool and proper brushes. A cyclone separator keeps the filter clean so suction does not fade. The catch is fit: attachments come in 1-1/4, 1-7/8 and 2-1/2 inch sizes, and a part that is the wrong size is useless. This guide picks seven worth buying by job and by hose size, with exact part numbers.
        </p>

