        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What size are shop vac attachments?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Almost all shop vac attachments fit one of three nominal hose diameters: 1-1/4 inch, 1-7/8 inch or 2-1/2 inch. Small 1 to 2.5 gallon vacs and detailing hoses use 1-1/4 inch, mid-size vacs use 1-7/8 inch and most large vacs use 2-1/2 inch. Measure the outside of your wand or hose cuff to check before you order.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are shop vac attachments universal?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not fully. Friction-fit tools of the same diameter usually fit across Shop-Vac, Craftsman, Vacmaster and WORKSHOP vacs, though fit can be loose or tight. RIDGID's locking tools lock only on RIDGID hoses, and its 1-1/4 inch car kit is sized for its own hose. Hose cuffs that plug into the vac vary by brand and are the least interchangeable part.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best shop vac attachment kit?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For a 1-7/8 or 2-1/2 inch vac, the RIDGID VT2575 (catalog 32703): a 12-piece kit with two stainless steel locking wands, a floor nozzle with squeegee, brush and carpet inserts, a claw nozzle, crevice tool, dusting brush and adapters for both hose sizes. On a budget, the WORKSHOP WS25054A adds five key tools for 2-1/2 inch hoses.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What attachment is best for cleaning a car?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A car kit with a flexible crevice tool, soft and stiff brushes and a claw nozzle. The RIDGID VT2534 comes with its own 10 foot 1-1/4 inch hose, which is light and reaches into footwells. For a 2-1/2 inch vac, the WORKSHOP WS25052A plugs straight on with a flexible crevice tool, a soft triangle brush and a claw nozzle.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I need a cyclone separator for my shop vac?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                If the vac sees sawdust, drywall dust or a lot of fine debris, yes. A separator like the Dust Deputy DIY or Dustopper PRO drops most dust into a bucket before it reaches the filter, so suction holds up and filters last much longer. If you mostly vacuum water or loose debris, it adds little.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Dust Deputy or Dustopper: which is better?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Choose by hose size and space rather than efficiency claims, which we have not seen independently tested side by side. The Dust Deputy DIY has a 1.5 inch inlet and adapters that suit small vacs; the Dust Deputy 2.5 DIY suits 2-1/2 inch hoses. The Dustopper PRO is a low bucket lid for 2-1/2 inch hoses that snaps on with no cutting.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How do I connect a shop vac to a sander or saw?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Use a hose kit with fittings sized to tool ports, such as the POWERTEC 70376. It has a 10 foot 1-1/2 inch ID hose, quick-connect fittings from 3/4 inch to 1-1/2 inch ID and a 2-1/4 to 2-1/2 inch adapter. Measure your tool's port and your vac's inlet first, since sizes vary by brand.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
